### [F-002] IIS Webroot Write Access + SeImpersonatePrivilege Escalation

| | |
|---|---|
| **Severity** | Critical |
| **CWE** | CWE-732 (Incorrect Permission Assignment), CWE-269 (Improper Privilege Management) |
| **Affected** | `C:\inetpub\wwwroot`, IIS AppPool `DefaultAppPool` service account, Windows Server 2022 build 10.0.20348.4052 |

**Description**
The `JOB\developers` group has Full Control (F) on the IIS web root (`C:\inetpub\wwwroot`), with Object Inherit / Container Inherit flags. The compromised user `jack.black` is a member of `developers`, allowing arbitrary file upload to the web server. Combined with the IIS AppPool account having `SeImpersonatePrivilege` enabled, this creates a direct path to SYSTEM via token-impersonation attacks (JuicyPotato / PrintSpoofer / RoguePotato / GodPotato).

**Impact**
Webshell uploaded as `jack.black`, executed as `IIS AppPool\DefaultAppPool` with `SeImpersonatePrivilege` — a direct path to SYSTEM, persistent backdoor access, arbitrary code execution in the IIS context, and the ability to tamper with legitimate site content.

